      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your concern about the costs and inconvenience of an ER visit, but the sooner you consult a healthcare professional, the better. While some mild cases of Bell's Palsy can improve over a few days without further intervention, it's essential to rule out other serious conditions or complications. If possible, make an appointment with your primary care doctor as soon as you can. In the meantime, you can often apply warm compresses to the affected side of your face and try to rest as much as possible.",
