      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're welcome. The key signs that warrant an immediate trip to the emergency room include: \n1. Sudden onset of severe pain around the affected area.\n2. Weakness, numbness, or loss of movement in other parts of your body, aside from your face.\n3. Slurred speaking or difficulties with swallowing. \n4. Swelling in the face or neck that worsens over time.\n5. Persistent inability to close your eye or severe drooping that remains and doesn't improve. \nIf any of these symptoms develop or if your condition worsens over the next few days to weeks, seek medical attention immediately. For now, if any of these symptoms appear, it's crucial to go to the ER right away. It’s better to be safe and ensure nothing more serious is at play.",
